2. What it does NOT cover: the archived 2021 files stay unclaimed
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Every other file on this branch is the archived 2021 work, unchanged. The
repository was published without a licence (no LICENSE file at any commit
before this branch; GitHub reported "license": null). interpreter/package.json
lists its contributors as Grant Van Horn, Jess Sullivan, Benjamin Hoffman and
"Visipedia et al."; per-line authorship is not established.

Nothing on this branch licenses, relicenses or claims those files. They stay
exactly as they were: unlicensed, with any rights held by their authors. For
the 2021 files changed in 2026 (listed above), only the 2026 changes are
Apache-2.0; the 2021 text in them stays unlicensed as described here.

3. Magenta.js and Google's web-audio-recognition code (Apache-2.0)
------------------------------------------------------------------

Parts of the 2021 browser spectrogram code on this branch are adapted from
Apache-2.0 code by Google:

  - interpreter/src/spectrogram_utils.ts: stft, magSpectrogram, hannWindow,
    padConstant, padReflect, padCenterToLength, frame, applyWindow, fft, mag,
    pow and the inner _powerToDb follow Magenta.js
    music/src/core/audio_utils.ts (https://github.com/magenta/magenta-js)
    in names, structure and comments.
    Magenta.js: Copyright 2018 Google Inc. All Rights Reserved.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  - interpreter/src/audio_utils.ts and interpreter/src/audio_loading_utils.ts
    carry their own notice, kept verbatim in those files: "based on
    https://github.com/google/web-audio-recognition/blob/librosa-compat ...
    Copyright 2018 Google Inc. All Rights Reserved. Licensed under the Apache
    License, Version 2.0".

This NOTICE credits that work; the copyright and licence of the adapted code
remain Google's. The 2026 revival does not run or modify this browser code
(the TensorFlow.js page at /classify/server is out of the revival's scope).

4. The model is not here and is not Merlin's
--------------------------------------------

No model file is in this repository, at 940f10c2 or on this branch: the 2021
TFLite and TensorFlow.js files were never committed. The revival serves a
2026 reconstruction instead: the xoruby-2026 ml/recipe2021 model (ONNX; three
classes: blue_jay, northern_cardinal, black_capped_chickadee), trained in 2026
on public Wikimedia Commons audio. It is not Merlin's model, weights, data or
code. It is loaded at run time from an xoruby-2026 checkout (MIT licence) and
is not redistributed here.

